+    // 1907N: disabled. This Android 13 optimization adds 2 extra buffers
+    // (kDisplaySyncExtraBuffer) to any HW-composer-consumed stream (i.e. the live preview
+    // SurfaceView, active in both Photo and Video mode). Front-camera Video mode hangs on
+    // every capture app tested (Aperture/CameraX, a third-party GCam port, and the legacy
+    // AOSP Camera2 app) with a real ISP hardware DMA error (CAM_A DMA_ERR_ST) on every frame;
+    // Photo mode and rear-camera video are both unaffected. A real LOS19.1 build with a
+    // byte-identical kernel and vendor camera HAL blob (confirmed via git history - neither
+    // has ever been modified) does not hit this error and records fine; LOS19.1's
+    // frameworks/av predates this extra-buffer mechanism entirely. Leading theory: Video
+    // mode has two continuously-active streams (preview + encoder) sharing the same MTK ISP
+    // DMA/FBC hardware path for this sensor, and the extra 2 preview buffers push the
+    // aggregate buffer/DMA demand past whatever the closed vivo/MTK HAL's normal_video
+    // scenario was actually validated against - Photo mode's second stream (JPEG) is not
+    // continuously active, so it never reaches the same aggregate demand. Disabling this
+    // reverts buffer-count negotiation to the LOS19.1-equivalent (proven-working) behavior,
+    // at the cost of losing this Android 13 preview-smoothness optimization. Not yet
+    // confirmed on real hardware - this is the next build/flash/test cycle's hypothesis.
+    if ((res = configureConsumerQueueLocked(false /*allowPreviewRespace*/)) != OK) {
         return res;
     }
 
